WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:03.830
If you want to hear about the secret activity
Jill Tuck participated in behind the scenes

00:00:03.830 --> 00:00:07.200
and the meaning behind it, then stick around
to the end of this video.

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:16.080
Jigsaw, the most notorious anti-hero of the Saw
franchise was driven to commit his crimes

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:19.160
based on what he saw as injustices in his
past.

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:22.500
Perhaps the one person who was most closely
tied to the events that inspired his actions

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:24.160
was his then wife, Jill Tuck-Kramer.

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:25.980
And in today’s lesson we are discussing

00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:29.720
why you should never marry an older man for
his money because he might turn out to be a serial killer

00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:33.309
-- no -- we’re gonna be analysing the character
of Jill Tuck, and to do so, we’ve gotta

00:00:33.309 --> 00:00:35.940
take it back to the first mention of Jigsaw’s
girl.

00:00:41.359 --> 00:00:44.989
Jill Tuck-Kramer was a doctor who sought to
help drug addicts by running a recovery center

00:00:44.989 --> 00:00:48.449
called Homeward Bound Clinic, whose motto,
“Cherish Your Life” was adopted from a

00:00:48.449 --> 00:00:50.460
phrase created by Jill’s husband, John Kramer.

00:00:50.460 --> 00:00:53.640
It’s likely that the two were drawn to each
other because of their mutual interest in

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:57.389
helping people improve their lives, but they
would ultimately find differing methods of

00:00:57.389 --> 00:00:58.389
going about it.

00:00:58.389 --> 00:01:02.170
But John loved his wife, so he took her on
picnics and recorded her on a video camera

00:01:02.170 --> 00:01:05.479
in the park… cause, I guess that’s what
you do when you’re in love.

00:01:05.479 --> 00:01:08.520
In 1995, Jill becomes pregnant with their
first child.

00:01:08.520 --> 00:01:11.810
John started to have doubts about the effectiveness
of the treatments his wife was administering

00:01:11.810 --> 00:01:13.350
to drug addicts at Homeward Bound Clinic.

00:01:13.350 --> 00:01:16.939
As he was waiting for her to get done working
one evening, he witnessed a fight break out

00:01:16.939 --> 00:01:20.330
when one of the patients, a man named Cecil
Adams, gets fed up with how long he’s been

00:01:20.330 --> 00:01:21.939
standing by in the waiting room.

00:01:21.939 --> 00:01:22.939
“**** man!

00:01:22.940 --> 00:01:25.500
I’ve been waiting for three ****ing hours!”

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:26.380
"Shut the **** up!"

00:01:26.380 --> 00:01:26.900
"You shut up!"

00:01:27.080 --> 00:01:29.580
Actual footage of me trying to get on the
Hagrid ride.

00:01:29.580 --> 00:01:33.060
Jill tries to stop the brawl, but John has
to step in when Cecil looks like he’s about to

00:01:33.070 --> 00:01:34.100
pull out a knife.

00:01:34.109 --> 00:01:36.439
John is able to get him to calm down and put
it away.

00:01:36.439 --> 00:01:40.020
As the due date of the baby gets closer, John
calls Jill into his workshop and shows her

00:01:40.020 --> 00:01:44.090
a series of gifts he’s been working on:
including a clock built with a 300 year old

00:01:44.090 --> 00:01:47.890
mechanism, meant to be symbolic of their long
lasting relationship, a crib for the incoming

00:01:47.890 --> 00:01:51.310
baby, and a cute version of Billy the Puppet
in the form of a children’s toy, which I’m

00:01:51.310 --> 00:01:55.390
not sure why this hasn’t become a merchandising
phenomenon, LIONSGATE, but I digress.

00:01:55.390 --> 00:01:59.420
The entire pregnancy was perfectly planned
by John, from the baby’s birth in the Chinese

00:01:59.420 --> 00:02:02.930
Year of the Pig, to the name Gideon, which
is also the name of the first building John

00:02:02.930 --> 00:02:04.990
ever owned: The Gideon Meat Packing Plant.

00:02:04.990 --> 00:02:08.670
I wouldn’t personally name my kid after
a meat packing plant, but the name may have

00:02:08.670 --> 00:02:12.990
been drawn from the Hebrew name Gidon which
means hero or judge, both of which John saw

00:02:12.990 --> 00:02:14.100
himself as.

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:17.700
One day during an ultrasound, John pulls out
the old camcorder and they make a home video

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:18.700
for Gideon.

00:02:20.380 --> 00:02:22.520
“Lean inside. There we go.

00:02:23.240 --> 00:02:24.120
Here we are.”

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:25.360
“Hey Gideon.”

00:02:25.420 --> 00:02:26.700
“Here’s our little happy family.

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:29.580
We love you son, we’re waiting for you.”

00:02:29.590 --> 00:02:32.260
Why does that come off as incredibly creepy?

00:02:32.260 --> 00:02:35.800
Oh right, because this is the same guy who
made video tapes for all the people he tortured

00:02:35.800 --> 00:02:36.300
and murdered.

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:39.940
The event that would set that all in motion
would soon come, during another evening at

00:02:39.940 --> 00:02:40.970
Homeward Bound Clinic.

00:02:40.970 --> 00:02:44.880
Jill, who was now seven months pregnant, was
finishing up and about to go home when Cecil

00:02:44.880 --> 00:02:47.090
appears and claims he forgot his jacket inside.

00:02:47.090 --> 00:02:50.650
When she goes to give it to him, he forces
his way in and holds her at knifepoint so

00:02:50.650 --> 00:02:52.720
he can steal more medications to relieve his
fix.

00:02:52.720 --> 00:02:55.860
In doing so, he slams the door into her pregnant
belly.

00:02:55.860 --> 00:02:58.760
"AHHHHHHHHHHHHHH!!!!!!!!!"

00:02:58.760 --> 00:03:01.990
John knows something is wrong when he sees
Cecil fleeing the building, and goes in to

00:03:01.990 --> 00:03:03.750
find his wife collapsed on the floor.

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:07.260
He rushes her to a hospital, but the baby
is unable to be saved, which would put a huge

00:03:07.260 --> 00:03:08.590
strain on their relationship.

00:03:08.590 --> 00:03:12.950
The reason this tore them apart is not just
related to emotional trauma, but also their

00:03:12.950 --> 00:03:14.670
ideals, which were drifting apart.

00:03:14.670 --> 00:03:18.600
Jill believed that her treatment, which included
medication and therapy, was the best solution,

00:03:18.600 --> 00:03:21.370
but John was becoming convinced that this
was not enough.

00:03:22.760 --> 00:03:25.400
“All I wanted to do was help them.”

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:26.740
“You can’t help them.

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:30.560
They have to help themselves.”

00:03:30.740 --> 00:03:34.080
...especially after seeing Jill’s treatment
was ineffective in some patients, such as

00:03:34.090 --> 00:03:36.690
Cecil Adams, and another woman named Amanda
Young.

00:03:36.690 --> 00:03:40.590
Meanwhile, Jill was left alone to cope with
the loss, while John fell into a deep depression

00:03:40.590 --> 00:03:42.380
and withdrew himself from the marriage.

00:03:42.380 --> 00:03:43.830
“He blamed me.

00:03:45.400 --> 00:03:47.380
I don’t think he could ever forgive me.”

00:03:47.390 --> 00:03:50.680
In what may have been a last ditch effort
by Jill to pull John out of this depression,

00:03:50.680 --> 00:03:54.570
she shows up to his workshop with his lawyer,
Art Blank, who tries to convince John to come

00:03:54.570 --> 00:03:57.560
back and return to his work, which involved
helping families in need.

00:03:57.600 --> 00:03:58.100
"Uhm..

00:03:59.640 --> 00:04:00.760
if you're homeless...

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:03.700
...just buy a house."

00:04:05.560 --> 00:04:09.060
John is unwilling to cooperate; he forfeits
his shares of the company to Jill, who ended

00:04:09.070 --> 00:04:11.870
up shutting down the Gideon Meat Packing Plant
for unknown reasons.

00:04:11.870 --> 00:04:15.600
At some point they got divorced, and between
that and the fact that Seinfeld was ending,

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:18.850
she dropped the “Kramer” hyphenation off
of her last name, and went back to just being

00:04:18.850 --> 00:04:19.850
Jill Tuck.

00:04:19.850 --> 00:04:23.540
Sometime around then, Jill’s family abandons
a pig farm they owned in the countryside due

00:04:23.540 --> 00:04:25.790
to an outbreak of Aujesky’s disease.

00:04:25.790 --> 00:04:29.260
After dealing with that, Jill hears that her
ex-husband had attempted suicide, so being

00:04:29.260 --> 00:04:32.870
the forgiving caregiver that she is, she seeks
him out to try to talk with him.

00:04:32.870 --> 00:04:36.760
When she goes into the workshop, she finds
reconnaissance photos of Cecil, perhaps confirming

00:04:36.760 --> 00:04:39.630
her suspicions that John had something to
do with his death.

00:04:39.630 --> 00:04:43.290
When she found John, she claimed that he was
now a different person, seeing the horrors

00:04:43.290 --> 00:04:45.070
of what his new work consisted of.

00:04:45.070 --> 00:04:49.000
She discovers the truth, that John had turned
Cecil into the first victim of his so called

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:50.210
rehabilitation.

00:04:50.210 --> 00:04:53.890
Jill doesn’t approve of his methods, causing
him to go ballistic and destroy the clock

00:04:53.890 --> 00:04:58.220
he had once made for her, the symbol of their
long lasting connection was now gone.

00:05:05.680 --> 00:05:07.400
“Now you don’t come back.

00:05:08.380 --> 00:05:11.220
You do it for yourself if you can’t do it
for me.”

00:05:12.360 --> 00:05:14.000
“I lost him too.”

00:05:14.600 --> 00:05:18.340
The two would separate for several years after
that, until John came back to the clinic to

00:05:18.340 --> 00:05:21.180
confront his ex on her methods one more time.

00:05:28.520 --> 00:05:32.460
After becoming Jigsaw, John would spend a
good amount of his time trying to rehabilitate

00:05:32.460 --> 00:05:36.650
the ex patients of the Homeward Bound Clinic,
the most notable of which was Amanda Young.

00:05:36.650 --> 00:05:40.530
After John believed she was clean, following
his test of her in 2004, he brought her back

00:05:40.530 --> 00:05:44.280
to Homeward Bound as proof to Jill that his
rehabilitation methods were working.

00:05:44.280 --> 00:05:48.010
Jill had previously dropped Amanda from her
list of patients, thinking she was a lost

00:05:48.010 --> 00:05:52.120
cause, so she was shocked to see that her
ex-husband was able to turn Amanda into an

00:05:52.120 --> 00:05:53.120
ex-addict.

00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:54.440
At least it appeared that way.

00:05:54.440 --> 00:05:58.080
This encounter did not immediately change
Jill’s mind about John’s work, but rather,

00:05:58.080 --> 00:06:01.450
would become something she would look back
on in a few years while contemplating whether

00:06:01.450 --> 00:06:02.730
or not to help carry out his legacy.

00:06:02.730 --> 00:06:07.150
The couple would have one more meeting that
we know of in April of 2006, not long before

00:06:07.150 --> 00:06:09.220
the main events of Saw III and IV.

00:06:09.220 --> 00:06:12.810
John and his followers were busy setting up
the final two games of Jigsaw’s life, one

00:06:12.810 --> 00:06:16.250
of which involves him testing a doctor and
her husband at Gideon Meat Packing Plant,

00:06:16.250 --> 00:06:18.470
which sat abandoned ever since Jill shut it
down.

00:06:18.470 --> 00:06:21.770
She was still the owner of the building though,
and turns up one day to beg John to put an

00:06:21.770 --> 00:06:23.400
end to his work as Jigsaw.

00:06:23.400 --> 00:06:27.610
He ignores her request, and instead promises
her a way out when everything is over with.

00:06:27.610 --> 00:06:28.820
Roll it.

00:06:29.800 --> 00:06:32.140
“And I have something for you.”

00:06:39.080 --> 00:06:40.800
“What’s this for?”

00:06:43.840 --> 00:06:49.800
“When the time’s right, you’ll know
what to do.”

00:06:49.810 --> 00:06:51.820
That would be their final encounter in person.

00:06:51.820 --> 00:06:55.420
Shortly before John’s death, the police
investigate Jill as a suspected accomplice

00:06:55.420 --> 00:06:59.090
after discovering she was in possession of
the Billy doll and tricycle used in the videos

00:06:59.090 --> 00:07:00.790
left to many of Jigsaw’s victims.

00:07:00.790 --> 00:07:04.790
The investigation wrecks havoc on her life
-- she ends up being interrogated for… according

00:07:04.790 --> 00:07:06.090
to her, 100s of hours.

00:07:06.090 --> 00:07:08.990
She also claims many things were taken from
her home for the investigation.

00:07:08.990 --> 00:07:13.370
On April 28th, Jigsaw is running two games,
one of which is a test for Officer Daniel

00:07:13.370 --> 00:07:14.370
Rigg.

00:07:14.370 --> 00:07:17.620
The FBI Agents, Strahm and Perez are following
him, and they arrive at his home, where the

00:07:17.620 --> 00:07:19.320
first phase of the test took place.

00:07:19.320 --> 00:07:23.340
The walls are covered with photos of Jigsaw’s
victims, but there’s one wild card -- Jill

00:07:23.340 --> 00:07:24.790
Tuck can also be seen in the photos.

00:07:24.790 --> 00:07:28.840
And I love how John took the time to get these
candid photos of his ex wife out and about

00:07:28.840 --> 00:07:29.840
in town.

00:07:29.840 --> 00:07:32.210
I mean, I know they got divorced, but he seriously
didn’t have one photo?

00:07:32.210 --> 00:07:34.699
He could have printed out her MySpace
picture or something!

00:07:34.699 --> 00:07:39.050
Kind of weird to secretly take photos of your
ex who is way younger than you.

00:07:39.050 --> 00:07:42.840
Anyway, this leads Strahm and Perez to confront
her at her work and bring her in for even

00:07:42.840 --> 00:07:43.890
more questioning.

00:07:43.890 --> 00:07:47.139
This time instead of just asking about John,
they were also asking about her.

00:07:47.139 --> 00:07:50.520
As the end of the games draw near, Strahm
gets more desperate for the answers that have

00:07:50.520 --> 00:07:51.520
eluded him.

00:07:51.520 --> 00:07:55.320
He threatens to pin charges on her and also
physically pins her against the wall to intimidate

00:07:55.320 --> 00:07:55.820
her.

00:07:55.820 --> 00:07:58.800
Jill doesn't have much to tell but she does
tell him about her divorce.

00:07:58.800 --> 00:08:02.490
This eventually leads Strahm to ask about
the location of Gideon Meat Packing Plant,

00:08:02.490 --> 00:08:05.270
John's first building where the two games were taking place.

00:08:05.270 --> 00:08:09.010
She does not realize that she's sending Strahm
into a trap of his own, which is facilitated

00:08:09.010 --> 00:08:11.870
by Jigsaw's actual accomplice, Detective Mark
Hoffman.

00:08:11.870 --> 00:08:15.430
Tuck and Hoffman would establish a sort of
rivalry that ramped up after John's death

00:08:15.430 --> 00:08:19.120
on the 28th. Hoffman wanted Jill out of the
picture so that he could have complete control

00:08:19.120 --> 00:08:22.900
over Jigsaw's legacy and make judgements on
his own, while Jill was growing disdain for

00:08:22.900 --> 00:08:27.190
Hoffman because he was starting to act against
John's final wishes by taking over the games

00:08:27.190 --> 00:08:31.160
John didn’t have time to carry out in life
for selfish reasons in order to increase his

00:08:31.160 --> 00:08:31.660
power.

00:08:31.660 --> 00:08:34.399
Despite the fact that they couldn’t make
their marriage work, Jill still had enough

00:08:34.399 --> 00:08:38.159
respect for John to want to see that his final
requests are carried out properly, and Hoffman

00:08:38.159 --> 00:08:39.339
was getting in the way of that.

00:08:39.340 --> 00:08:43.200
Not long after, news of John Kramer's death
and identity as Jigsaw went public, and she

00:08:43.200 --> 00:08:47.160
finds herself surrounded by news articles
claiming to know and understand both sides

00:08:47.170 --> 00:08:50.860
of John Kramer, which must have been surreal
because the only one to truly know both sides

00:08:50.860 --> 00:08:51.860
of him was her.

00:08:51.860 --> 00:08:55.759
The media also speculated on her involvement
even though she had not actually been involved

00:08:55.759 --> 00:08:56.759
up to that point.

00:08:56.759 --> 00:09:00.089
She noticed she was being followed, and that
didn’t surprise her at first, because of

00:09:00.089 --> 00:09:03.660
the initial wave of media attention, but she
soon grew paranoid that someone was stalking her.

00:09:03.840 --> 00:09:07.240
She meets with John’s executor, the man
responsible for paying out John’s will,

00:09:07.240 --> 00:09:11.040
who shows her a VHS containing one final message
from her late ex husband.

00:09:11.040 --> 00:09:12.300
Roll that tape.

00:09:12.640 --> 00:09:16.949
“If you’re watching this Jill, I’m long
gone from this world.

00:09:16.949 --> 00:09:20.279
You are my heart, you always have been.

00:09:20.280 --> 00:09:22.140
You always will be.”

00:09:22.140 --> 00:09:24.019
Things not to say to your ex for 500.

00:09:24.019 --> 00:09:27.600
It’s important to note John’s clothing
and hairstyle during this tape, which tells

00:09:27.600 --> 00:09:31.540
us that it was recorded just before the main
events in Saw III, a game that potentially

00:09:31.540 --> 00:09:34.759
could have ended with John being killed or
possibly imprisoned for the remainder of his

00:09:34.760 --> 00:09:35.260
life.

00:09:35.260 --> 00:09:38.580
Even though they were not speaking at the
time, John still has Jill’s best interests

00:09:38.589 --> 00:09:42.360
at the top of his mind, even as he is busy
making preparations for the most complex and

00:09:42.360 --> 00:09:43.810
dangerous game he’s ever held.

00:09:43.810 --> 00:09:47.019
He goes on to tell her that he blames himself
for what happened to Gideon at the Homeward

00:09:47.019 --> 00:09:50.810
Bound Clinic, and that he encouraged her work
at the time, even when he sensed danger on

00:09:50.810 --> 00:09:51.400
the horizon.

00:09:51.400 --> 00:09:55.319
This is a bit different than his stance immediately
after the miscarriage, where he was upset

00:09:55.319 --> 00:09:58.579
that she could not understand how the flaws
in her treatment methods led to this.

00:09:58.579 --> 00:10:02.170
Had John blamed himself from the beginning,
I think it’s entirely possible that Jill

00:10:02.170 --> 00:10:06.019
would have reacted more receptively, and perhaps
they would not have gotten divorced and things

00:10:06.019 --> 00:10:07.129
may have gone much differently.

00:10:07.129 --> 00:10:09.899
He leaves her a box and tells her she’ll
know what to do with the contents.

00:10:09.899 --> 00:10:14.120
That’s when she remembers her final encounter
with John, and uses the key he gave her, which

00:10:14.120 --> 00:10:17.309
she’s kept on her this entire time, perhaps
a sign that she still had kind of a place

00:10:17.309 --> 00:10:21.360
in her heart for John even after the divorce
and even after learning he’d become a serial

00:10:21.360 --> 00:10:24.839
killer -- and I think that small amount of
love she had left for him started to influence

00:10:24.839 --> 00:10:26.290
her decisions going forward.

00:10:26.290 --> 00:10:29.629
She decides not to take the contents out of
the box in front of this guy though.

00:10:29.629 --> 00:10:30.730
And I don’t blame her.

00:10:30.730 --> 00:10:31.749
Look at those eyes.

00:10:31.749 --> 00:10:35.360
“What was in the box? What’s in the box?”

00:10:35.360 --> 00:10:39.499
The box contained six numbered envelopes,
one labeled parcel, and a number of related

00:10:39.499 --> 00:10:43.589
materials and instructions including one of
Jigsaw’s most iconic traps... but Jill would

00:10:43.589 --> 00:10:46.760
wisely wait until she knew she was alone before
opening them.

00:10:56.480 --> 00:11:00.300
After receiving the box from John, Jill still
could not shake the feeling that someone was

00:11:00.300 --> 00:11:04.501
stalking her and goes to the FBI headquarters
to inform the head of the investigation, but

00:11:04.501 --> 00:11:07.340
for some reason he just wouldn’t stop asking
for pictures of Spiderman.

00:11:11.060 --> 00:11:11.740
"You serious?"

00:11:11.820 --> 00:11:12.940
Nah that’s not him.

00:11:12.949 --> 00:11:16.730
She tells him she believes that Agent Strahm, the
man who interrogated her, is responsible.

00:11:16.730 --> 00:11:20.879
She later opens the envelopes and finds they
contain profiles on six more victims who are

00:11:20.879 --> 00:11:22.470
to be tested in upcoming games.

00:11:22.470 --> 00:11:26.309
The first five are players in the trial of
William Easton, an insurance mogul who once

00:11:26.309 --> 00:11:27.970
rejected John’s request for coverage.

00:11:27.970 --> 00:11:29.639
(That’s the main game in Saw 6.)

00:11:29.639 --> 00:11:33.680
The sixth envelope contains a profile on Detective
Hoffman, who has now become the successor

00:11:33.680 --> 00:11:34.680
to Jigsaw.

00:11:34.680 --> 00:11:38.179
Hoffman thinks that he and Jill are the only
ones left to carry out the rest of John’s

00:11:38.179 --> 00:11:42.410
work, but Jill has been given a bit more information
than him, which again, is an important illustration

00:11:42.410 --> 00:11:44.290
of where John’s trust really lies.

00:11:44.290 --> 00:11:47.649
Jill knows that there is one other disciple
who has been working behind the scenes for

00:11:47.649 --> 00:11:52.199
a long time now and decides to keep this information
to herself, because she senses that John did

00:11:52.199 --> 00:11:53.629
not fully trust Hoffman.

00:11:53.629 --> 00:11:56.930
Eventually, Hoffman shows up at the clinic
and demands she forfeit the envelopes to him

00:11:56.930 --> 00:11:58.999
so that he can be the one to run the next
game.

00:11:58.999 --> 00:12:02.370
He wants to work alone from now on so that
he can get away with as much foul play as

00:12:02.370 --> 00:12:03.370
he wants.

00:12:03.370 --> 00:12:07.059
She only hands over envelopes 1-5, completely
hiding the existence of a sixth file.

00:12:07.059 --> 00:12:11.060
Later, Jill receives a visit from a reporter
named Pamela Jenkins who delivers a note found

00:12:11.060 --> 00:12:14.700
at Gideon Meat Packing Plant, the main location
from Saw III where John was killed.

00:12:14.700 --> 00:12:18.380
The note reads: “Amanda - You were with
Cecil the night Jill lost Gideon.

00:12:18.380 --> 00:12:19.559
You killed their child.

00:12:19.559 --> 00:12:22.459
You know it and I know it, so do exactly as
I say.

00:12:22.460 --> 00:12:24.440
Kill Lynn Denlon or I will tell John what
you did.”

00:12:24.440 --> 00:12:26.520
Now this gets a little bit confusing, but here's

00:12:26.620 --> 00:12:27.960
why it’s a big deal for Jill.

00:12:27.960 --> 00:12:31.420
For some time, she been thinking back on her
conversation with John and Amanda.

00:12:31.420 --> 00:12:34.920
That was the first time that Jill started
to maybe believe that John’s method of helping

00:12:34.920 --> 00:12:37.579
people -- using the traps and games was superior.

00:12:37.579 --> 00:12:41.339
But when Amanda went off the rails and failed
her final test by killing Lynn Denlon, an

00:12:41.339 --> 00:12:45.059
event that ultimately ended up leading to
John’s death, Jill lost faith in his methods.

00:12:45.059 --> 00:12:50.160
But this note, if genuine, proves that Amanda
was blackmailed, so maybe she really was rehabilitated,

00:12:50.160 --> 00:12:53.350
and only killed Lynn Denlon to protect her
secret about being with Cecil.

00:12:53.350 --> 00:12:55.900
If this note is indeed from Hoffman, then that

00:12:55.910 --> 00:13:00.260
also proves he has broken the rules in order
to take Amanda out and become the only disciple

00:13:00.279 --> 00:13:04.029
of Jigsaw, and if that is the case, he’s
dangerous and needs to be stopped.

00:13:04.029 --> 00:13:07.949
Jill knows she probably can’t defeat Hoffman
on her own, so she plays her trump card and

00:13:07.949 --> 00:13:12.319
pays a visit to the disciple that she knows
about, but Hoffman does not; Jigsaw’s greatest

00:13:12.319 --> 00:13:17.139
asset: Dr. Lawrence Gordon, the winner of
the bathroom game two years ago in 2004.

00:13:17.139 --> 00:13:20.500
Jill goes to the hospital that Gordon now
works at and delivers the parcel into the

00:13:20.500 --> 00:13:21.699
slot on his door.

00:13:21.699 --> 00:13:25.569
It contains a tape left behind by John, telling
Gordon to act immediately if anything should

00:13:25.569 --> 00:13:26.569
happen to Jill.

00:13:26.569 --> 00:13:29.829
With the peace of mind that she will at least
be avenged if she fails, Jill gathers the

00:13:29.829 --> 00:13:33.430
last of the materials John had left her in
his will, and shows up to the location of

00:13:33.430 --> 00:13:36.220
the next game to administer Hoffman’s final
test.

00:13:36.220 --> 00:13:39.809
She manages to subdue him by running an electric
current into the back of his chair and leaving

00:13:39.809 --> 00:13:42.949
the note that he had once used to blackmail
Amanda on the desk.

00:13:42.949 --> 00:13:46.749
Once Hoffman read the note and realized that
someone else knew his secret, she activated

00:13:46.749 --> 00:13:50.639
the electricity to incapacitate him, strapped
him to the chair, and brought out the final

00:13:50.639 --> 00:13:54.759
item left to her in the box from John’s
will, the reverse bear trap, which was famously

00:13:54.759 --> 00:13:56.809
used to test Amanda back in 2004.

00:13:56.809 --> 00:14:00.201
Jill was finally about to carry out John’s
final wish, but because she wasn’t there

00:14:00.201 --> 00:14:04.129
with him during the final years of his life,
she never got to hear this important piece

00:14:04.129 --> 00:14:05.120
of advice:

00:14:06.640 --> 00:14:09.980
“You’re assuming this is going to play
out the way you want it.”

00:14:09.980 --> 00:14:11.959
“I assume nothing.”

00:14:11.959 --> 00:14:16.600
Jill did not anticipate the possibility of
Hoffman escaping the trap, and when he does,

00:14:16.600 --> 00:14:20.199
she is forced to run for it and hide out until
Hoffman leaves the building, taking the reverse

00:14:20.199 --> 00:14:21.421
bear trap with him.

00:14:21.421 --> 00:14:25.809
Both Mark Hoffman and Jill Tuck go dark for
almost a year, and all the while Jill is haunted

00:14:25.809 --> 00:14:29.861
by nightmares of Hoffman capturing her and
brutally ending her life as revenge for her

00:14:29.861 --> 00:14:30.861
messing up his jaw.

00:14:30.861 --> 00:14:34.869
Still, she is able to stay hidden for a long
time until March of 2007, when she hears about

00:14:34.869 --> 00:14:37.560
a new Jigsaw trap taking place in public.

00:14:37.820 --> 00:14:38.980
"Hello Brad.

00:14:39.780 --> 00:14:40.780
Hello Ryan.

00:14:41.580 --> 00:14:43.020
I want to play a game."

00:14:43.129 --> 00:14:46.319
With the knowledge that Hoffman is active
again, her paranoia gets the better of her

00:14:46.319 --> 00:14:48.779
and she goes to the police station seeking
protection.

00:14:48.779 --> 00:14:52.360
Which is honestly kind of insane because her
husband was responsible for the death of like

00:14:52.360 --> 00:14:55.829
5 of their cops and… let’s not forget
the creation of Hoffman who is like the biggest

00:14:55.829 --> 00:14:59.700
psycho ever so… pretty ballsy of Jill to
trust the cops at this point, but apparently

00:14:59.700 --> 00:15:02.850
she’s got a good feeling about this guy,
Matt Gibson from Internal Affairs.

00:15:02.850 --> 00:15:06.779
She tells him that Hoffman is Jigsaw’s successor
and secret accomplice and offers what she

00:15:06.779 --> 00:15:08.439
knows in exchange for protection and immunity.

00:15:08.440 --> 00:15:12.580
He puts her in a safehouse, but after Hoffman
demonstrates that he knows she's there,

00:15:12.580 --> 00:15:16.680
"This was sent here addressed to Jill. Hoffman knows our location"

00:15:16.680 --> 00:15:17.440
"Godd*mnit."

00:15:17.660 --> 00:15:20.080
...moves her to a high security holding cell for her
protection.

00:15:20.089 --> 00:15:23.699
None of these precautions, however, are enough
to stop Hoffman from getting to her.

00:15:23.699 --> 00:15:27.190
He holds the body of an assistant to the window
in order to get the guards to open the door,

00:15:27.190 --> 00:15:30.370
and takes them out to bring himself face to
face with Jill Tuck.

00:15:30.370 --> 00:15:32.070
“I’ve been looking for you.”

00:15:32.070 --> 00:15:36.329
In a last ditch effort, she stabs him in the
neck and runs to hide in the evidence room.

00:15:36.329 --> 00:15:39.779
He still finds her though, and in a cruel
twist of fate, straps her to the very same

00:15:39.779 --> 00:15:42.939
chair where she had left him to die less than
one year ago.

00:15:42.939 --> 00:15:47.350
Unlike Amanda and Hoffman, Jill is not able
to escape from the reverse bear trap, and

00:15:47.350 --> 00:15:48.080
meets her demise.

00:15:48.080 --> 00:15:50.780
“Game Over.”

00:15:51.620 --> 00:15:56.560
However, her backup plan did work, as Lawrence
Gordon was quickly able to avenge her, so

00:15:56.560 --> 00:16:00.280
she was still able to be a part of the plan
to carry out John’s final wish, even in

00:16:00.280 --> 00:16:00.780
death.

00:16:00.780 --> 00:16:03.700
I think Jill Tuck actually has one of the
best character arcs in the series.

00:16:03.709 --> 00:16:07.420
When we meet her she’s very convinced that
her way of helping people using medication

00:16:07.420 --> 00:16:10.829
and traditional therapy is the only way to
help these troubled people overcome their

00:16:10.829 --> 00:16:11.340
addictions.

00:16:11.340 --> 00:16:14.480
John’s philosophy is that going through
an immense amount of suffering can help someone

00:16:14.489 --> 00:16:18.269
see the light, and although John isn’t intentionally
putting her through any suffering, she does

00:16:18.269 --> 00:16:21.749
suffer the loss of her unborn son and the
loss of her marriage, and this eventually

00:16:21.749 --> 00:16:26.569
leads to her realization that John’s judgements,
although oftentimes cruel, could be effective,

00:16:26.569 --> 00:16:30.249
and she ends up playing a key part in bringing
down the series’s most evil villain as a

00:16:30.249 --> 00:16:31.249
result.

00:16:31.249 --> 00:16:34.910
It’s kind of easy to overlook her character
arc, because her story is chopped up and distributed

00:16:34.910 --> 00:16:39.360
intermittently throughout Saws 4-7 and rarely
becomes the main focus, but hopefully this

00:16:39.360 --> 00:16:43.110
Horror History gave you a better idea of
why did what she did behind the scenes and

00:16:43.110 --> 00:16:44.999
what her character means for the franchise.

00:16:45.000 --> 00:16:45.500
SO.

00:16:45.500 --> 00:16:49.600
Your homework is to let me know in the comments
who I should cover next on Horror History,

00:16:49.600 --> 00:16:52.839
and make sure you check out that playlist
on the left for more episodes including other

00:16:52.839 --> 00:16:53.839
Saw characters.

00:16:53.839 --> 00:16:58.290
Remember to subscribe to CZsWorld for new
horrors every week, ring that deathbell for

00:16:58.290 --> 00:17:01.100
notifications and I’ll see you in the next
one.

00:17:01.100 --> 00:17:03.620
Assuming we both survive.

